yest":"November 13: cooler than 80% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>66\u00b0F</strong> was the 16th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 85 since 1940, the coolest since 2000. The normal high for the date is 74\u00b0F, and the record is 95\u00b0F (2013). The low of <strong>58\u00b0F</strong> was the 3rd warmest November 13 low of 86 since 1940.","t_rec":"Burbank has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Burbank's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Burbank has set <strong class=\"sig\">7 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 114 that chance alone would give, and <strong>103 record highs</strong>, close to the 115 that chance alone would give. The 1970s hold the most record highs of any decade (76). Burbank's all-time high is 114\u00b0F, on July 6, 2018.","t_chg":"Burbank's nights got warmer. Its days didn't.","p_chg":"Across 79 complete years: Burbank's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.69\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.56 to +0.81), about +5.9\u00b0F since 1940. Burbank's average high shows no clear change: +0.14\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.01 to +0.29) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero.","t_mon":"Lows rose in all 12 months. Highs rose in 2 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Burbank's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.22 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 14.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1983 (39.77 in); the driest, 2002 (0.26 in). Burbank almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 12 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}